        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ecology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Ecology is the study of interactions between organisms and their environment. It operates at nested levels of organization and intersects every other biological and earth science. The fundamental insight: species don't exist in isolation — they exist in webs of relationships, constrained by physical environment and shaped by evolution."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ecology:00-overview, git-history:ecology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ecology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ecology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ecology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ecology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    ECOLOGY LEVELS OF ORGANIZATION                |\n|                                                                  |\n|  ORGANISM     Individual physiology, behavior, life history      |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  POPULATION   Single species in a place; dynamics over time      |\n|               (birth, death, immigration, emigration)            |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  COMMUNITY    Multiple species interacting                       |\n|               (predation, competition, mutualism)                |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  ECOSYSTEM    Community + abiotic environment                    |\n|               (energy flow + nutrient cycling)                   |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  LANDSCAPE    Mosaic of ecosystems                               |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  BIOME        Major vegetation/climate zone (global scale)       |\n|      |                                                           |\n|      v                                                           |\n|  BIOSPHERE    All life on Earth + Earth systems                  |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
