      "text": "## The Niche Concept"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#016",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ecology:00-overview, git-history:ecology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ecology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ecology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ecology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ecology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "G. E. Hutchinson's (1957) fundamental niche: n-dimensional hypervolume in environmental space within which a species can persist. Realized niche = subset occupied given competition, predation."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#017",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ecology:00-overview, git-history:ecology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:ecology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ecology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "ecology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ecology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Formally: the fundamental niche is the feasible region in ℝⁿ defined by n inequality constraints (one per environmental variable). Each constraint is a range: species survives when temperature ∈ [T_min, T_max], humidity ∈ [H_min, H_max], etc. The intersection of all n constraint sets is the niche hypervolume — exactly a convex polytope in the n-dimensional parameter space if constraints are independent. The realized niche is the feasible region further reduced by biotic constraints (competition, predation) — a constraint satisfaction problem where abiotic constraints define the feasible region and biotic interactions carve out additional infeasible subsets."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#018",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:ecology:00-overview, git-history:ecology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "ecology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
